|***************************************************************************
| y32a.ibs * IBIS 5.0 Model 
| 16Gb DDR5 SDRAM - Die Revision "A" 
| This Model is valid for Commercial Temperature Range 0C<=Tc<=95C 
|
| Valid for up to 4800 Gbps DDR5 operation 
|
| Part Number       VDD/VDDQ    Architecture   Package
| -----------       --------    ------------   -------
| MT60B4G4HB        1.1V/1.1V   4Gb   x 4      78-Ball VFBGA
| MT60B2G8HB        1.1V/1.1V   2Gb   x 8      78-Ball VFBGA
| MT60B1G16HC       1.1V/1.1V   1Gb   x 16    102-Ball VFBGA
|***************************************************************************
|
[IBIS Ver]    5.0
[File Name]   y32a.ibs
[Date]        4/21/2021
[File Rev]    2.2
[Source]      From silicon level SPICE model at Micron Technology, Inc.
              For support contact your local Micron FAE/Sales contacts
              (more information at https://www.micron.com/support/sales-network)
|
[Notes]       Revision History:
              Rev 2.2: 4/21/2021
               - Matched C_comp with 4/13/2020 measurements
               - Updated CA, CLK and CS models with specific (per ODT)
                 C_comp values
              Rev 2.1: 1/8/2021
               - Matched C_comp with 7/28/2020 measurements
              Rev 2.0.2: 12/14/2020
               - Reordered TDQS and DM_TDQS selectors to have *ODT_OFF* the
                 first (default) model
              Rev 2.0.1: 9/9/2020
               - Updated Sparse Matrix package models for bith x8 and x16
              Rev 2.0: 7/14/2020
               - Matched C_comp with 4/6/2020 measurements
               - Matched IV curves with 3/18/2020 measurements
               - Renamed INPUT* models to CA_INPUT*
               - Renamed CLKIN* models to CLK_INPUT*
               - Added CS_INPUT* models
              Rev 1.1: 10/30/2019
               - Added component MT60B1G16HC (x16)
               - Updated part numbers MT60B4G4HB (x4) and MT60B2G8HB (x8)
              Rev 1.0: 6/14/2019
               - Added INPUT_ODT240_4800 and CLKIN_ODT240_4800 models
               - Updated VT tables for DQ model family
               - Updated ALERT model
               - Updated part numbers
              Rev 0.1: 6/10/2019
               - Initial release
|
              Notes:
               - This IBIS file uses the Submodel keyword to model the
                 DDR5 On-die Termination(ODT) characteristics. 
               - The C_comp value in the DQ I/O model is set to match the 
                 input state of the DQ I/O as measured from the HSPICE model.
                 The C_comp value decreases in the DQ/DQS Input ODT models.
               - L_pin values in the Pin sections are loop inductance and 
                 include the mutual inductance to appropriate POWER/GND
                 return paths.  POWER/GND parasitics are modeled in the 
                 Package Models.
               - Typ and slow corner V-t curves in the following DQ* models 
                 are shifted relative to strong corner V-t curve 
                 to contain all 3 corners within appropriate V-t window
|
                 Models        Typ       Slow      V-t duration
                 --------      ------    ------    ------------
                 DQ_*_4800     -100ps    -255ps     300ps
                 ALERT          -67ps    -175ps     300ps
|
               - Due to the shift in typ and slow corner, the V-t curves
                 may overlap each other. This does not effect the accuracy 
                 of the IBIS data.
               - DBI is not supported yet for y32a
               - The NF_DQ Model is for Non-functioning pins in the x4
                 package
               - IBIS Quality Specification 2.0 Summary:
                 IQ Score: IQ3MSX
                 See Micron IBIS Model Quality Report and Quality Checklist 
                 for full IQ details
|                     
